The bug occurs because the error handling is performed after the error is logged, without checking if the error is significant. This can lead to misleading log entries indicating a failure when the error might not require any action, especially during the driver unload process.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
err = mlx5_cmd_check(dev, err, in, out);
if (err) {
    mlx5_core_warn(dev, "func_id 0x%x, npages %d, err %d\n", func_id, npages, err);
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves calling `mlx5_cmd_check` before logging the error. This function verifies whether the returned error is an actual error that needs to be handled, ensuring that only significant errors are logged, thus preventing misleading log entries during the driver unload process.

